# The Dockerfile copies only pyproject.toml, src/ and PRIVACY.md. Everything here is
# context uploaded to the Docker daemon on every build for nothing.
#
# app/ is the reason this file exists: it holds the Xcode project and, since the
# Android client landed, a Gradle project whose build output reaches ~700 MB
# once anyone compiles in this worktree. None of it is needed to build a Python
# image.
#
# Deliberately a denylist rather than a `*` + `!src/` allowlist: if a future
# Dockerfile copies something new, a denylist keeps working, whereas a
# mis-specified allowlist breaks the deploy.

app/
venv/
data/
tmp/
previews/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.agents/

__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.env
